#!/bin/sh
cat <<'EOF'

  RabbitOS public sandbox guide
  -----------------------------
  First steps
    1. Copy a repo to work on:   repos      then   cp -r /workspace/rabbit-web ~/work/
    2. Look around:              cd, ls, cat, rg "text" .
    3. Public chain ledger:      ledger
    4. Public research data:     curl -fsS "https://app.rabbitsoftware.io/api/data" | jq     (read-only; datasets, columns, row counts)
                                 curl -fsS "https://app.rabbitsoftware.io/api/data/research_records?limit=50" | jq
                                 add  &format=csv  or  &format=ndjson ; page with the nextCursor value as  &cursor=...

  Coding agents (bring your own key; /workspace is read-only, work in ~/work)
    gemini     needs GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY)  - paste it in the "API keys" drawer before you start
    claude     needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY                   - same drawer
    copilot    needs a GitHub Copilot subscription. Either run  /login  inside copilot
               (device-code flow: open the URL it prints in YOUR browser), or paste a
               fine-grained token with the "Copilot Requests" permission into the drawer
               (COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN). Use a low-limit or short-lived key; this box is shared.
    The page's "Start my default agent" button types the agent name; press Enter yourself.

  PowerShell and the network
    pwsh             start PowerShell 7 (the login shell stays bash; type  exit  to leave). Invoke-WebRequest / Invoke-RestMethod work, but only
                     through the same allowlist as curl (HTTPS, the hosts below, mostly read-only).
    rabbit-net status   show the normal, allowlisted connection (no proxy, no VPN)
    rabbit-net check    HTTPS reachability test (HEAD, 5 s timeout) of the allowed hosts only
    Not installed on purpose: ping/ICMP, DNS lookup tools, traceroute, nmap, netcat and other scanners. Only HTTPS to named hosts can leave this box,
    so those tools could not work anyway and would only be useful for probing other people's machines. Run them on your own PC instead
    (RabbitNet PowerShell module in rabbit-web/scripts/powershell, see docs/rabbitos.md).

  Common commands
    cd DIR   ls -la   cat FILE   rg PATTERN   git status / git log   node FILE.js   python3 FILE.py

  Limits
    Login shell is bash (pwsh is available). 1/4 vCPU, 1 GiB RAM, small disk. Ends after 10 idle
    minutes or 30 minutes total; nothing is kept. Network: package registries, public
    GitHub, api.anthropic.com, generativelanguage.googleapis.com, Copilot hosts, RabbitOS chain and data hub (reads only).

EOF
